time yesterday, we **would have restored** the old portrait.”"],"skill":"meaning"},{"title":"Past condition, present result","explanation":"A mixed conditional can link an unreal past condition to a present result. The if-clause stays past perfect, but the present result normally uses would + base verb. Explicit time words help the reader follow the link.","pattern":"If I **had studied** medicine, I **would be** a doctor now.","commonMistakes":["Do not force have into a present result merely because the condition is past."],"examples":["Complete the present result of a mixed conditional: “If she had prepared the visitor guide yesterday, she **would be** free now.”","Complete the present result of a mixed conditional: “If she had restored the old portrait yesterday, she **would be** free now.”"],"skill":"contrast"},{"title":"Present condition, past result","explanation":"A continuing hypothetical state can explain an unreal past result. Use if + past simple for the imagined state and would have + participle for the past result. Match each clause to its own time instead of memorising one fixed pair.","pattern":"If I **were** more organised, I **would have remembered** yesterday.","commonMistakes":["The label mixed describes the time relationship, not an error in tense consistency."],"examples":["Complete the past result of a mixed conditional: “If I were more organised, I **would have prepared** the visitor guide yesterday.”","Complete the past result of a mixed conditional: “If I were more organised, I **would have restored** the old portrait yesterday.”"],"skill":"application"}],"tips":[],"source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-third-conditionals"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"chapter":{"introduction":["Look back at an unreal past and connect past conditions with present consequences.","The form tells you how to build the sentence; the context tells you why that